Trading Model Spec — QT Core
1) Core Premise
This is a Quarterly Theory timing model built around:
Fractal time cycles
True Opens
SMT / Sequential SMT
PDArray reactions
Intermarket relative strength / weakness
News-timed manipulation and distribution
The model assumes that time organizes price delivery, and that the highest-probability trades come when price reaches a meaningful opening price or PDArray during the correct quarter of the cycle, with SSMT confirming the narrative.
2) Time Framework
Fractal cycle structure
Year = 4 quarters
Month = 4 quarters
Week = 4 quarters
Day = 4 quarters
Session = 4 quarters
Daily cycle used
Q1: 6:00 PM – 12:00 AM
Q2: 12:00 AM – 6:00 AM
Q3: 6:00 AM – 12:00 PM
Q4: 12:00 PM – 6:00 PM
Core rule
Q2 open is the True Open of the cycle.
3) True Open Framework
Main idea
True Opens are the backbone of the model. Price is judged by how it behaves around, through, and back around these opens.
True Open bias logic
Bullish condition: price is below the cycle’s True Open, or raids below it, then confirms higher
Bearish condition: inverse
Stored True Open references
True Year Open: April open / first Monday of April open
True Month Open: second Monday / second full week open
True Week Open: Tuesday open, with variant reference of Monday 6:00 PM
True Day Open: 12:00 AM
Session True Opens: London 1:30 AM, NY AM 7:30 AM, NY PM 1:30 PM
Revolving True Open
Defined as the Q4 open of a cycle when SSMT is present between Q3→Q4 or Q4→Q1
Important for reversal models, especially Q4 reversals
