Q4: Distribution
Barometer rule
If Q1 expands, then Q2 likely consolidates
If Q1 consolidates, then Q2 likely expands
5) Bias Model
Bias is not taken from raw direction alone. It is built from the stack below:
Bias checklist
Where is price relative to the relevant True Open?
What quarter of the cycle is active?
Is the cycle behaving like AMDX or XAMD?
Has price interacted with a key PDArray?
Has SMT / SSMT confirmed manipulation or relative weakness?
Is there intermarket confirmation?
Is there a news-timing reason for manipulation or distribution?
A trade is strongest when multiple layers line up instead of relying on one isolated signal.
6) Setup Conditions
Base setup
A valid setup usually needs:
Price interaction with a True Open
Price reaching a key PDArray
Proper quarter timing
SMT or SSMT
Clear relative strength / weakness across correlated assets
Preferred environment
